and never came back.

264
00:27:17,928 --> 00:27:19,138
I thought

265
00:27:20,556 --> 00:27:21,890
things would get better with time.

266
00:27:32,234 --> 00:27:33,652
That she'd be okay

267
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,363
because she had me.

268
00:27:39,032 --> 00:27:40,242
But I was wrong.

269
00:27:52,588 --> 00:27:53,589
Mom.

270
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:19,615
Mom!

271
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:39,468
I was completely useless.

272
00:28:44,014 --> 00:28:45,681
Why aren't you watching
where you're going?

273
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:47,768
Why did you cross the road
without checking the traffic light?

274
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:55,442
I'm always too late.

275
00:28:59,988 --> 00:29:01,573
I end up driving everyone away.

276
00:29:08,247 --> 00:29:10,499
How is any of that your fault?

277
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:12,167
They were hurting so much...

278
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:16,964
and I failed to see it.

279
00:29:20,425 --> 00:29:22,803
I don't think I deserve
to have anyone by my side.

280
00:29:28,016 --> 00:29:29,226
At first

281
00:29:30,227 --> 00:29:32,729
I thought you were so cold.

282
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:36,024
But now, I know.

283
00:29:37,693 --> 00:29:39,069
You aren't cold.

284
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:43,782
You're just terrified.

285
00:29:47,369 --> 00:29:48,620
Terrified of losing people again.

286
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:51,540
Terrified of being too late.

287
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:57,796
When things get tough,
it's okay to admit it.

288
00:29:58,213 --> 00:30:01,508
It's okay to let yourself
fall apart sometimes.

289
00:30:04,678 --> 00:30:06,888
I'll stay by your side to the end.

290
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:12,019
If I mean anything to you...

291
00:30:14,730 --> 00:30:16,023
don't let me go this time.

292
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:53,851
Hi, Mi-mi. Have you been busy lately?

293
00:30:53,852 --> 00:30:56,103
How about we go for a drive
this weekend? Are you in?

294
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:57,521
Did I get dumped?

295
00:30:57,522 --> 00:30:59,273
I thought we really clicked that day.

296
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:01,776
To find myself

297
00:31:01,777 --> 00:31:04,236
Lost in childhood dreams

298
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:06,072
I'll go away

299
00:31:06,073 --> 00:31:07,616
Beyond the blue sky

300
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:11,787
Jeez.

301
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:14,331
Goodness.

302
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:17,666
Leaving someone on read
has its limits.

303
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:19,502
If you play hard to get,
you'll end up getting played.

304
00:31:19,503 --> 00:31:22,338
This is how I keep them
thinking about me all day.

305
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:24,383
It reels them in even faster.

306
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:27,260
Reel him in? Oh, please.

307
00:31:28,345 --> 00:31:29,970
You're the one who got reeled in.

308
00:31:29,971 --> 00:31:33,682
I'm not into guys
who give up this easily anyway.

309
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:35,685
If it's bothering you that much

310
00:31:36,311 --> 00:31:37,437
text him first.

311
00:31:39,356 --> 00:31:40,357
Me?

312
00:31:41,191 --> 00:31:42,192
Why would I do that?

313
00:31:43,485 --> 00:31:45,278
You treat relationships like a game.

314
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:46,988
No wonder you're single.

315
00:31:49,074 --> 00:31:50,617
QUICK DELIVERY

316
00:31:57,791 --> 00:32:01,670
Do you know why you guys are hooked
like helpless fish caught in her net?

317
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:03,171
It's the impatience.

318
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:05,256
Your desperation.

319
00:32:05,257 --> 00:32:07,007
Right, the impatience...

320
00:32:07,008 --> 00:32:08,760
I'm too desperate.

321
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:10,928
My impatience.

322
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,263
Right when you're ready to give up

323
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:14,683
she'll toss you
another crumb with a text message.

324
00:32:19,354 --> 00:32:20,896
What are you up to?

325
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:22,189
MI-MI

326
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:24,484
That's when you stop!

327
00:32:25,026 --> 00:32:26,903
Don't even open it. Don't reply.

328
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:29,156
- Why not?
- Treat her exactly the same way.

329
00:32:29,489 --> 00:32:30,532
The same way?

330
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:32,868
Goodness.

331
00:32:36,288 --> 00:32:38,123
Gosh, what do I do?

332
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:57,309
My beloved Appello family.

333
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:02,981
A lot has been going on
at our company lately.

334
00:33:03,273 --> 00:33:05,192
I'm sure most of you have guessed

335
00:33:06,234 --> 00:33:07,736
but we are

336
00:33:08,778 --> 00:33:11,864
- in a crisis right now.
- What crisis?

337
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:14,492
With both our CEO
and our Planning Team Manager absent

338
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:17,953
who are we supposed to rely on?

339
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:22,625
In times like these,
we must stick together.

340
00:33:22,626 --> 00:33:26,754
We must protect the Appello we love.

341
00:33:26,755 --> 00:33:28,548
So who do we need right now?

342
00:33:30,050 --> 00:33:35,304
From here on out,
bring all important matters to me.

343
00:33:35,305 --> 00:33:37,973
For anything important,
you can rely on me.

344
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:39,100
If you have any...

345
00:33:41,311 --> 00:33:42,479
Hello, Mr. Kang.

346
00:33:42,979 --> 00:33:44,189
You're here, Mr. Kang.

347
00:33:46,316 --> 00:33:49,777
- Thanks, but I'm here now.
- Why...

348
00:33:49,778 --> 00:33:50,779
I'm glad you're here.

349
00:33:54,449 --> 00:33:57,159
Shall we all get to work?

350
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,286
- Yes!
- Yes!

351
00:34:01,581 --> 00:34:02,749
I meant well.

352
00:34:36,575 --> 00:34:38,242
HAN'S OFFICIAL KOREAN PARTNER

353
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:39,869
APPELLO WAS CHOSEN
AS HAN'S OFFICIAL PARTNER IN KOREA

354
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:42,080
We got it.

355
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:43,957
No way!

356
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,166
Check your email!

357
00:34:46,167 --> 00:34:47,876
- Did you see the notice?
- Yes!

358
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:49,045
Did we get it?

359
00:34:51,131 --> 00:34:52,799
Great job, everyone.

360
00:34:53,592 --> 00:34:55,093
Congratulations.

361
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:05,936
HAN'S OFFICIAL KOREAN PARTNER

362
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:07,438
HAN, FASHION'S HOTTEST ISSUE

363
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:09,356
SIGNS MOU
WITH THEIR KOREAN PARTNER, APPELLO

364
00:35:09,357 --> 00:35:10,482
SE:ON, GREAT LOSS
ON UPFRONT INVESTMENT

365
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:12,068
FAILED TO WIN OVER HAN,
SE CORP. MIGHT LOSE BILLIONS

366
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:14,153
SE:ON USERS, MASSIVE EXODUS

367
00:35:14,154 --> 00:35:15,362
Kim Han-cheol!

368
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:16,780
SE CORPORATION

369
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:19,575
Do you know how much we lost
because of you?

370
00:35:19,576 --> 00:35:21,285
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Whatever.

371
00:35:21,286 --> 00:35:22,787
I won't renew your contract.

372
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:26,833
- Sir.
- Jeez.

373
00:35:40,472 --> 00:35:43,933
I hope we get on well together,
Mr. Kang, my Korean business partner.

374
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:47,604
Thanks, Jeong-yeon.

375
00:35:48,146 --> 00:35:49,397
You helped a great deal.

376
00:35:51,316 --> 00:35:53,693
Director Kim's career is over.

377
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:58,239
Our joint operation
worked pretty well, right?

378
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,200
Yes.

379
00:36:01,785 --> 00:36:03,953
- Are you going back to France?
- Yes.

380
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:06,748
I'll prepare the launch
as soon as I get back.

381
00:36:07,082 --> 00:36:09,334
I'm serious about the Korean market.

382
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:12,629
I'll work hard
so everything works out smoothly.

383
00:36:12,754 --> 00:36:15,465
Can you send
one of your staff to France?

384
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,008
Sure.

385
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:25,767
By the way

386
00:36:26,935 --> 00:36:28,520
I still don't get it.

387
00:36:28,937 --> 00:36:31,439
Why did SE Corporation
copy the fake presentation?

388
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:36,319
You said you gave Mr. Choi
the actual proposal.

389
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:41,241
I have no idea.

390
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:44,202
I'd like to know too.

391
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:54,295
Ms. Han.

392
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:06,683
Can you spare me some time?

393
00:37:09,561 --> 00:37:13,648
NOT A CUSTOMER BUT A FAN
TASTEFUL SPACES IN KOREA

394
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:22,240
When did you prepare all this?

395
00:37:23,575 --> 00:37:27,412
I threw together some ideas I had
while working on the proposal.

396
00:37:27,871 --> 00:37:30,749
These aren't just some ideas
thrown together.

397
00:37:34,294 --> 00:37:38,798
I'm a huge fan of your brand,
so I did it out of admiration.

398
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:46,264
I also felt bad keeping you in check.

399
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:54,314
- Do you have plans for today?
- Me? No.

400
00:37:54,856 --> 00:37:56,316
Then have dinner with me.

401
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:00,278
I should pay you back.

402
00:38:02,197 --> 00:38:03,531
What food do you prefer?

403
00:38:04,365 --> 00:38:07,869
I eat pretty much anything.
What about you?

404
00:38:08,912 --> 00:38:11,790
- Korean cuisine.
- Korean cuisine...

405
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:17,337
Would you like to try a place
I recommend?

406
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:28,723
- It's hot.
- Thanks.

407
00:38:34,187 --> 00:38:37,732
They're all dishes my mom sent.

408
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:40,235
She's an incredible cook.

409
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:43,238
I'll enjoy this.

410
00:38:43,738 --> 00:38:45,365
I've been craving a home-cooked meal.

411
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:51,412
You don't have family here, do you?

412
00:38:54,833 --> 00:38:55,959
In my senior year of high school

413
00:38:57,085 --> 00:38:59,921
I went abroad to study alone
because my mom remarried.

414
00:39:00,421 --> 00:39:02,298
I didn't want to live
with my stepdad.

415
00:39:05,218 --> 00:39:06,469
We don't keep in touch now.

416
00:39:09,430 --> 00:39:11,266
Being alone must've been tough.

417
00:39:12,308 --> 00:39:14,102
But I didn't struggle
financially, though.

418
00:39:15,270 --> 00:39:17,939
- Thanks for the meal.
- I hope you like it.

419
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:24,611
- It's good.
- Isn't it?

420
00:39:24,612 --> 00:39:25,780
Please enjoy.

421
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:33,329
It's tasty.

422
00:39:38,835 --> 00:39:43,298
At first, my only goal
was to become the best employee.

423
00:39:44,299 --> 00:39:47,926
Once I got started,
I found myself trying to find my way.

424
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:50,388
It'll become clearer with time.

425
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:55,225
You said last time

426
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:59,856
that after your first brand failed,
you clearly saw what you could do.

427
00:40:01,357 --> 00:40:04,819
That stayed with me for a long time.

428
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:09,240
I plan to try whatever I can
and make failures too.

429
00:40:10,450 --> 00:40:11,451
That's a great idea.

430
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:21,002
I can see why Ha-gi chose you.

431
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:26,841
You're comforting
like a home-cooked meal.

432
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:28,551
And warm too.

433
00:40:31,596 --> 00:40:32,722
I am?

434
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:36,643
Ha-gi's a great guy for seeing that.

435
00:40:39,228 --> 00:40:40,438
Enough that I want to steal him.

436
00:40:42,607 --> 00:40:43,733
Sorry?

437
00:40:45,318 --> 00:40:46,569
So keep him close.

438
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:53,409
You scared me.

439
00:41:38,079 --> 00:41:39,080
Mom.

440
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,667
You liked this coffee brand.

441
00:41:46,254 --> 00:41:47,588
For my sake...

442
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:52,010
will you come and have a sip?

443
00:42:05,023 --> 00:42:06,983
I got your favorite.

444
00:42:08,526 --> 00:42:10,653
Why didn't you call ahead?

445
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:14,741
I was passing by and thought of you.

446
00:42:17,118 --> 00:42:18,286
Let's go inside. I'm starving.

447
00:42:27,336 --> 00:42:28,671
It's the anniversary
of my mom's passing.

448
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:31,924
This is your first time, right?

449
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:38,431
You're such a jerk.

450
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:46,814
Have you been doing this alone
without a word to me?

451
00:43:41,244 --> 00:43:42,245
I had no idea...

452
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:47,625
how much you suffered after I left.

453
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:56,384
Sorry for keeping it from you.

454
00:43:59,554 --> 00:44:00,721
I guess...

455
00:44:03,391 --> 00:44:05,476
I wasn't ready to face it myself.

456
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:11,858
But thanks to Ms. Da-reum

457
00:44:13,442 --> 00:44:14,735
I've changed my mind.

458
00:44:16,445 --> 00:44:17,822
I've decided to protect what's mine.

459
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:21,534
Everyone else has gone.

460
00:44:24,579 --> 00:44:25,955
But I really don't want to lose...

461
00:44:27,999 --> 00:44:29,417
both you and Ms. Da-reum.

462
00:44:49,896 --> 00:44:51,522
I hate myself.

463
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:55,818
I'm nothing compared to you.

464
00:45:01,908 --> 00:45:03,075
You two

465
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:05,953
mean a lot to me too.

466
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:10,833
So...

467
00:45:14,837 --> 00:45:16,464
Make Da-reum happy.

468
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:47,078
You'd better call me
for next year's anniversary.

469
00:45:48,496 --> 00:45:50,831
- I feel left out.
- Okay.

470
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:07,974
This is the contract
to Director Park's film.

471
00:46:08,307 --> 00:46:09,392
Congratulations, Chan.

472
00:46:31,539 --> 00:46:33,958
ACTOR: LEE CHAN

473
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:41,882
Whatever choice you make,
I want you to do

474
00:46:43,009 --> 00:46:44,343
what your heart tells you to do.

475
00:46:45,052 --> 00:46:46,762
Something for yourself.

476
00:46:56,522 --> 00:46:58,565
TEO

477
00:46:58,566 --> 00:47:00,443
We've been practicing together.

478
00:47:00,943 --> 00:47:03,571
Drop by if you'd like to see us.

479
00:47:19,754 --> 00:47:21,255
I guess I'm not over it.

480
00:47:22,256 --> 00:47:23,299
Not yet.

481
00:47:43,110 --> 00:47:44,195
Chan.

482
00:47:57,416 --> 00:47:58,626
Thanks a lot.

483
00:47:58,876 --> 00:48:01,962
I didn't think you'd actually visit.

484
00:48:05,841 --> 00:48:08,344
Why are you here? To cheer us on?

485
00:48:11,806 --> 00:48:13,224
There's still something
I'd like to do.

486
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:20,939
- Are we your sentimental backdrop?
- Don't.

487
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:23,651
What could you still want
when you were the first to leave?

488
00:48:26,654 --> 00:48:28,239
We never waited for you.

489
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:40,543
Then why did you leave
my part vacant?

490
00:48:46,340 --> 00:48:47,800
I get that you resent me.

491
00:48:48,551 --> 00:48:49,593
But

492
00:48:50,761 --> 00:48:51,929
I'm done running away.

493
00:48:53,514 --> 00:48:55,182
I know I'm asking a lot from you

494
00:48:56,767 --> 00:48:57,893
but one more time...

495
00:48:59,478 --> 00:49:00,688
Why don't we try again together

496
00:49:02,148 --> 00:49:03,941
just one more time?

497
00:49:10,781 --> 00:49:11,824
Together?

498
00:49:13,659 --> 00:49:15,911
Let's start again together.

499
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:18,831
Chan.

500
00:49:26,130 --> 00:49:27,131
Okay?

501
00:49:37,349 --> 00:49:38,392
Come on.

502
00:49:43,981 --> 00:49:45,149
Darn it.

503
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:48,777
Jeez.

504
00:50:08,380 --> 00:50:11,008
Why did you cancel my membership
when I still had classes left?

505
00:50:12,843 --> 00:50:14,011
You make me feel uncomfortable.

506
00:50:15,638 --> 00:50:17,681
- How so?
- You just do.

507
00:50:18,724 --> 00:50:19,808
I don't want to waste my energy.

508
00:50:21,894 --> 00:50:23,312
Let's call it quits, then.

509
00:50:25,105 --> 00:50:27,024
I'm done playing hard to get.

510
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:30,777
I'm capable and competent,
and I'm a good kisser.

511
00:50:30,778 --> 00:50:33,072
- I'm pretty good at it.
- What are you on about?

512
00:50:33,572 --> 00:50:36,784
I'll call when I want
and come to see you when I want.

513
00:50:39,620 --> 00:50:40,621
You win.

514
00:50:41,664 --> 00:50:42,873
I lost.

515
00:50:44,083 --> 00:50:46,835
You should quit playing games
and do the same.

516
00:50:47,127 --> 00:50:48,128
Sorry?

517
00:50:49,171 --> 00:50:50,172
What do you mean?

518
00:50:52,967 --> 00:50:54,009
Let's date.

519
00:51:22,121 --> 00:51:26,792
Don't you miss the other D.N.X guys?

520
00:51:29,420 --> 00:51:31,130
Would they miss me?

521
00:51:35,593 --> 00:51:37,553
I wouldn't know.

522
00:52:12,671 --> 00:52:14,840
Can I help you?

523
00:52:16,008 --> 00:52:17,468
- I brought your food.
- I see.

524
00:52:18,093 --> 00:52:19,887
Can you leave it over there?

525
00:52:20,638 --> 00:52:21,680
Sure.

526
00:52:22,389 --> 00:52:24,933
What about Roy's part?

527
00:52:27,102 --> 00:52:29,938
- Let's forget about it.
- He might come back.

528
00:52:30,189 --> 00:52:31,231
How?

529
00:52:31,607 --> 00:52:33,232
We don't even know
if he's dead or alive.

530
00:52:33,233 --> 00:52:34,360
He can't be dead.

531
00:52:39,531 --> 00:52:40,699
What if we look for him?

532
00:53:04,390 --> 00:53:05,723
You feel like

533
00:53:05,724 --> 00:53:09,269
you shouldn't meet the members,
even though you miss them, right?

534
00:53:11,105 --> 00:53:12,189
Is it because you feel bad?

535
00:53:14,233 --> 00:53:15,401
I ruined everything.

536
00:53:16,360 --> 00:53:17,653
That would be too shameless.

537
00:53:18,612 --> 00:53:20,739
Then go and show them how you feel.

538
00:53:22,783 --> 00:53:25,411
You can show
that you feel embarrassed

539
00:53:26,245 --> 00:53:27,538
or you could even cry.

540
00:53:29,456 --> 00:53:30,791
Why decide on your own?

541
00:53:32,042 --> 00:53:34,461
You don't know
if they'll curse you out

542
00:53:34,837 --> 00:53:37,089
or yell or take you back.

543
00:53:42,136 --> 00:53:43,137
I'm afraid.

544
00:53:54,148 --> 00:53:57,109
Do you know why I started deliveries
just to track you down?

545
00:53:59,945 --> 00:54:02,114
The thought of never seeing you again
and regretting it...

546
00:54:04,533 --> 00:54:07,453
was far scarier than the thought

547
00:54:08,579 --> 00:54:10,372
of getting disappointed
after meeting you.

548
00:54:12,750 --> 00:54:15,043
Your members might feel the same.

549
00:54:15,586 --> 00:54:19,256
They might hate you
but still miss you.

550
00:54:21,133 --> 00:54:22,634
If you really feel bad

551
00:54:24,595 --> 00:54:26,305
stop hiding

552
00:54:27,389 --> 00:54:30,017
and give the guys
a chance to hate you.

553
00:54:44,615 --> 00:54:47,159
I could cook better
if I had cookbooks.

554
00:54:47,868 --> 00:54:50,537
- Shall I buy you a few?
- No, thanks.

555
00:54:51,163 --> 00:54:53,165
MAGAZINE

556
00:54:56,460 --> 00:54:57,461
Wait.

557
00:55:00,756 --> 00:55:02,007
It's Ms. Han.

558
00:55:07,346 --> 00:55:08,806
I guess she gave an interview
while she was here.

559
00:55:11,850 --> 00:55:14,770
- Shall we go?
- Hold on. Let me read a bit more.

560
00:55:22,277 --> 00:55:24,822
HAN AND HER QUESTIONS

561
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:30,201
A NEW ENVIRONMENT
BRINGS NEW QUESTIONS

562
00:55:30,202 --> 00:55:33,288
THEY MADE ME STRONGER, FIRMER,
AND HELPED ME GROW

563
00:55:58,188 --> 00:55:59,897
Shall we go to the seaside
to watch the sun rise?

564
00:55:59,898 --> 00:56:02,109
I'd like that. Where would we go?

565
00:56:03,277 --> 00:56:05,445
We should go to the East Sea.

566
00:56:06,405 --> 00:56:08,115
Will we be
spending the night together?

567
00:56:10,951 --> 00:56:13,245
I guess so?

568
00:56:16,915 --> 00:56:17,916
A two-day trip?

569
00:56:26,675 --> 00:56:29,469
I really just want to see
the sunrise.

570
00:56:34,474 --> 00:56:35,601
I'll think about it.

571
00:56:37,811 --> 00:56:38,812
Okay.

572
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:42,399
You should get inside.

573
00:56:42,691 --> 00:56:43,692
Okay.

574
00:56:54,620 --> 00:56:56,163
It's late. You should go.

575
00:56:57,831 --> 00:56:58,832
Okay.

576
00:57:01,793 --> 00:57:03,587
- I'll go.
- Okay.

577
00:57:06,590 --> 00:57:08,383
- I should go.
- Yes.

578
00:57:27,194 --> 00:57:28,445
Mr. Kang.

579
00:57:29,988 --> 00:57:32,032
- Yes?
- My place

580
00:57:32,908 --> 00:57:34,910
might not have cats

581
00:57:35,953 --> 00:57:37,245
but there's something interesting.

582
00:57:39,122 --> 00:57:40,123
Would you like to see it?

583
00:57:44,753 --> 00:57:46,588
Something interesting?

584
00:57:55,639 --> 00:57:56,848
What could it be?

585
00:57:59,184 --> 00:58:00,268
I'm nervous now.

586
00:58:04,648 --> 00:58:05,899
Let's see.

587
00:58:27,587 --> 00:58:29,381
Try not to be too shocked.

588
00:58:32,467 --> 00:58:34,176
- Why show me this?
- What?

589
00:58:34,177 --> 00:58:36,263
You said your underwear was in here.

590
00:58:37,431 --> 00:58:38,724
So why...

591
00:58:53,905 --> 00:58:55,032
Ta-da.

592
00:59:01,788 --> 00:59:03,498
I LOVE LEE CHAN

593
00:59:03,790 --> 00:59:05,292
What is...

594
00:59:06,168 --> 00:59:08,210
What is all this?

595
00:59:08,211 --> 00:59:09,754
ALWAYS ON CHAN'S SIDE
FOREVER LEE CHAN

596
00:59:09,755 --> 00:59:11,882
It's a record of my 12 years

597
00:59:12,507 --> 00:59:13,550
as a fan.

598
00:59:24,895 --> 00:59:27,147
I didn't want to hide it anymore.

599
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:30,108
I wanted to show you
that this is who I am

600
00:59:30,942 --> 00:59:33,612
and the part of me that loves you

601
00:59:35,155 --> 00:59:36,364
is also a part of who I am.

602
00:59:42,788 --> 00:59:44,372
That's a weight off my shoulders.

603
00:59:44,790 --> 00:59:46,583
I can sleep at night at last.

604
00:59:49,336 --> 00:59:50,504
Gosh.

605
00:59:52,672 --> 00:59:54,090
What is it?

606
00:59:54,091 --> 00:59:58,261
You came clean first,
so I told you my secret too.

607
01:00:01,098 --> 01:00:02,432
I'm jealous, to be honest.

608
01:00:07,312 --> 01:00:09,314
I'll cut back on it now.

609
01:00:22,119 --> 01:00:24,287
I know he gave you
the will and energy to live.

610
01:00:27,207 --> 01:00:28,834
I should thank Chan.

611
01:00:32,838 --> 01:00:35,841
He brought us together.

612
01:00:40,428 --> 01:00:44,015
Does that mean my bias

613
01:00:45,433 --> 01:00:46,643
is you now?

614
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:49,080
- I'm heavy.
- Not at all.

615
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:37,896
I used to have an olive lemon shot
and Greek yogurt for breakfast.

616
01:03:37,897 --> 01:03:39,065
I quit that diet.

617
01:03:39,691 --> 01:03:40,859
Why?

618
01:03:41,192 --> 01:03:43,820
Cutting down on carbs
left me with no energy.

619
01:03:45,405 --> 01:03:46,948
Eat as much as you want.

620
01:03:47,532 --> 01:03:48,700
You weigh too little.

621
01:03:55,915 --> 01:03:58,626
Stop staring at me.
It's embarrassing.

622
01:04:00,879 --> 01:04:02,172
What were you thinking about?

623
01:04:02,422 --> 01:04:03,882
Will you stop it?

624
01:04:05,925 --> 01:04:07,844
It's not the first time
we've slept together.

625
01:04:08,845 --> 01:04:10,971
What are you talking about?

626
01:04:10,972 --> 01:04:12,265
When did we ever...

627
01:04:13,892 --> 01:04:15,101
After the welcome dinner.

628
01:04:15,727 --> 01:04:16,853
In my office.

629
01:04:34,537 --> 01:04:37,332
I tried to stay up all night,
but ended up falling asleep.

630
01:04:38,375 --> 01:04:39,542
No wonder.

631
01:04:40,251 --> 01:04:42,253
It all felt a bit familiar.

632
01:04:48,593 --> 01:04:50,178
I really had no idea then

633
01:04:51,471 --> 01:04:52,764
that this would happen.

634
01:05:07,445 --> 01:05:09,072
HAN AND HER QUESTIONS

635
01:05:10,657 --> 01:05:11,824
A NEW ENVIRONMENT
BRINGS NEW QUESTIONS

636
01:05:11,825 --> 01:05:13,201
THEY MADE ME STRONGER, FIRMER,
AND HELPED ME GROW

637
01:05:26,172 --> 01:05:28,924
ANY ADVICE FOR YOUNGER DESIGNERS
OR THOSE FINDING THEIR WAY?

638
01:05:28,925 --> 01:05:33,847
DON'T TRY TOO HARD TO CHANGE YOURSELF
CHANGE WHERE YOU ARE

639
01:05:42,772 --> 01:05:43,773
Mr. Kang.

640
01:05:45,400 --> 01:05:46,401
Yes?

641
01:05:49,237 --> 01:05:50,280
How about

642
01:05:51,489 --> 01:05:55,034
I apply to work in Paris?

643
01:06:16,973 --> 01:06:20,518
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

644
01:06:30,653 --> 01:06:32,864
I know it's a great opportunity
for Ms. Da-reum.

645
01:06:33,615 --> 01:06:34,948
But I want her to stay.

646
01:06:34,949 --> 01:06:36,951
Long-distance relationships
never work out.

647
01:06:37,494 --> 01:06:38,619
- Hey!
- My goodness!

648
01:06:38,620 --> 01:06:41,206
People there greet each other
with a kiss on the cheek.

649
01:06:42,123 --> 01:06:43,207
- One.
- Two.

650
01:06:43,208 --> 01:06:44,291
- Three.
- Four.

651
01:06:44,292 --> 01:06:45,709
- Five.
- Let's go!

652
01:06:45,710 --> 01:06:46,793
Come back, Roy.

653
01:06:46,794 --> 01:06:49,254
Let's stop running away.

654
01:06:49,255 --> 01:06:50,715
Instead of cheering you on

655
01:06:51,132 --> 01:06:53,176
I hated myself for feeling so petty.

656
01:06:54,427 --> 01:06:55,553
It felt like it was about me.

657
01:06:55,720 --> 01:06:57,514
You may be saying it to your fans

658
01:06:57,805 --> 01:07:00,474
but it's what I wanted to say to you.

659
01:07:00,475 --> 01:07:01,643
You won't let go

660
01:07:02,060 --> 01:07:03,770
just because I'm leaving, will you?
